</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F4.fig3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.04212v1/PKX_at_H8_batch_idx_190_token50_train_steps_6610.png" id="S3.F4.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:165/127;" width="165" height="127" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F4.fig4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.04212v1/PK_at_H8_batch_idx_209_6619.png" id="S3.F4.g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:165/131;" width="165" height="131" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F4.fig5" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.04212v1/X_at_batch_idx_209_train_steps_6619.png" id="S3.F4.g5" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:165/133;" width="165" height="133" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F4.fig6" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.04212v1/PKX_at_H8_batch_idx_209_token718_train_steps_6619.png" id="S3.F4.g6" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:165/125;" width="165" height="125" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span><math id="S3.F4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{P}}{\mathbf{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐏𝐊</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{P}}{\mathbf{K}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.F4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.F4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbf{P}}{\mathbf{K}})[T]^{\top}{\mathbf{X}}[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐏𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{P}}{\mathbf{K}})[T]^{\top}{\mathbf{X}}[T]</annotation></semantics></math> at different batch indices and training steps. (c) and (f) show that <math id="S3.F4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbf{P}}{\mathbf{K}})[T]^{\top}{\mathbf{X}}[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐏𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{P}}{\mathbf{K}})[T]^{\top}{\mathbf{X}}[T]</annotation></semantics></math> for different tokens and training steps have some similar columns in input features 546 and 678.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The gradient of the query projection matrix, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d{\mathbf{W}}^{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d{\mathbf{W}}^{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, is given by the outer product of the input features <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the query gradient <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d{\mathbf{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐐</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d{\mathbf{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The difference between the high-precision (<math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="hp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">hp</annotation></semantics></math>) and low-precision (<math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="lp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">lp</annotation></semantics></math>) gradients for <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{W}}^{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{W}}^{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d{\mathbf{W}}^{Q}_{hp}-d{\mathbf{W}}^{Q}_{lp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mi>Q</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mi>Q</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d{\mathbf{W}}^{Q}_{hp}-d{\mathbf{W}}^{Q}_{lp}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(d{\mathbf{Q}}_{hp}-d{\mathbf{Q}}_{lp})^{\top}{\mathbf{X}}=\alpha({\mathbf{P}}{\mathbf{K}})^{\top}\mathrm{diag}({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp}){\mathbf{X}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐏𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(d{\mathbf{Q}}_{hp}-d{\mathbf{Q}}_{lp})^{\top}{\mathbf{X}}=\alpha({\mathbf{P}}{\mathbf{K}})^{\top}\mathrm{diag}({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp}){\mathbf{X}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\sum\nolimits_{T=1}^{N}({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]\cdot({\mathbf{P}}{\mathbf{K}})[T]^{\top}{\mathbf{X}}[T]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐏𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\sum\nolimits_{T=1}^{N}({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]\cdot({\mathbf{P}}{\mathbf{K}})[T]^{\top}{\mathbf{X}}[T],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbf{P}}{\mathbf{K}})[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐏𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{P}}{\mathbf{K}})[T]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{X}}[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{X}}[T]</annotation></semantics></math> are the <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>-th row vectors of their matrices. This equation shows that the total gradient error is a weighted sum of rank-1 matrices, with weights given by the error in <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\delta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜹</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\delta}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Similar Low-rank Updates of Weight Cause Training Failure</h5>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#S3.F4" title="In Analysis of the Error between High and Low Precision Gradients ‣ 3.3.1 Cause 1. Similar Low-Rank Matrices Bias Weight Updates ‣ 3.3 The Root Causes of Training Failure ‣ 3 Root Causes of Instability in Flash Attention ‣ Why Low-Precision Transformer Training Fails: An Analysis on Flash Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, the rows of <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{P}}{\mathbf{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐏𝐊</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{P}}{\mathbf{K}}</annotation></semantics></math> (panels a, d) and <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> (panels b, e) exhibit strong structural similarity across different training steps and token positions. This implies that the resulting rank-1 matrices, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbf{P}}{\mathbf{K}})[T]^{\top}{\mathbf{X}}[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐏𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{P}}{\mathbf{K}})[T]^{\top}{\mathbf{X}}[T]</annotation></semantics></math>, are also highly similar to one another. For instance, <a href="#S3.F4" title="In Analysis of the Error between High and Low Precision Gradients ‣ 3.3.1 Cause 1. Similar Low-Rank Matrices Bias Weight Updates ‣ 3.3 The Root Causes of Training Failure ‣ 3 Root Causes of Instability in Flash Attention ‣ Why Low-Precision Transformer Training Fails: An Analysis on Flash Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> (panels c, f) shows this similarity for tokens 50 and 718 at training steps 6610 and 6619, respectively. Because these rank-1 error components are structurally consistent, we can approximate the total gradient difference as</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d{\mathbf{W}}^{Q}_{hp}-d{\mathbf{W}}^{Q}_{lp}\approx\alpha\sum\nolimits_{T=1}^{N}({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]{\mathbf{R}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mi>Q</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mi>Q</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐑</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d{\mathbf{W}}^{Q}_{hp}-d{\mathbf{W}}^{Q}_{lp}\approx\alpha\sum\nolimits_{T=1}^{N}({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]{\mathbf{R}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐑</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the common low-rank structure emerging across different tokens and training steps.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Eqn.(<a href="#S3.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ Similar Low-rank Updates of Weight Cause Training Failure ‣ 3.3.1 Cause 1. Similar Low-Rank Matrices Bias Weight Updates ‣ 3.3 The Root Causes of Training Failure ‣ 3 Root Causes of Instability in Flash Attention ‣ Why Low-Precision Transformer Training Fails: An Analysis on Flash Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) shows that the accumulation of the low-rank error direction <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐑</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> is governed by the scalar term <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{T=1}^{N}({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{T=1}^{N}({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]</annotation></semantics></math>. If this sum is biased towards non-zero values, the error across different training steps will accumulate rather than cancel out. We track the cumulative sum of <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{T=1}^{N}({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{T=1}^{N}({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]</annotation></semantics></math> over a sequence of training steps (6580 to 6680) leading up to the failure, as shown in <a href="#S3.F5" title="In Similar Low-rank Updates of Weight Cause Training Failure ‣ 3.3.1 Cause 1. Similar Low-Rank Matrices Bias Weight Updates ‣ 3.3 The Root Causes of Training Failure ‣ 3 Root Causes of Instability in Flash Attention ‣ Why Low-Precision Transformer Training Fails: An Analysis on Flash Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>(a). The plot reveals that this sum is consistently positive, indicating a systematic bias. This bias causes the error in the low-rank direction <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐑</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> to compound with each training step. Because <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐑</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> is also similar for different steps, this ultimately corrupts the weight updates, increases the spectral norm (<a href="#A3.F9" title="In Explanation on Dealing Negative Repeated Row Maximum ‣ Appendix C Design Considerations for Mitigating Biased Rounding Error in Flash Attention ‣ Why Low-Precision Transformer Training Fails: An Analysis on Flash Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) and activations <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rybakov et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, and causes the training failure (refer to <a href="#Thmclaim2" title="Claim 2. ‣ Similar Low-rank Updates of Weight Cause Training Failure ‣ 3.3.1 Cause 1. Similar Low-Rank Matrices Bias Weight Updates ‣ 3.3 The Root Causes of Training Failure ‣ 3 Root Causes of Instability in Flash Attention ‣ Why Low-Precision Transformer Training Fails: An Analysis on Flash Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Claim</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). The following section finds the root cause of this positive bias by analyzing the weights and gradients at training step 6619, a point of significant positive contribution identified in <a href="#S3.F5" title="In Similar Low-rank Updates of Weight Cause Training Failure ‣ 3.3.1 Cause 1. Similar Low-Rank Matrices Bias Weight Updates ‣ 3.3 The Root Causes of Training Failure ‣ 3 Root Causes of Instability in Flash Attention ‣ Why Low-Precision Transformer Training Fails: An Analysis on Flash Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>(a).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="118.14" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 118.14" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,118.14) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(13.75,0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.7 L 0 113.43 C 0 116.03 2.11 118.14 4.7 118.14 L 517.79 118.14 C 520.39 118.14 522.5 116.03 522.5 113.43 L 522.5 4.7 C 522.5 2.11 520.39 0 517.79 0 L 4.7 0 C 2.11 0 0 2.11 0 4.7 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2FFFF;" fill="#F2FFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.55 4.7 L 0.55 113.43 C 0.55 115.73 2.41 117.59 4.7 117.59 L 517.79 117.59 C 520.09 117.59 521.94 115.73 521.94 113.43 L 521.94 4.7 C 521.94 2.41 520.09 0.55 517.79 0.55 L 4.7 0.55 C 2.41 0.55 0.55 2.41 0.55 4.7 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.41 97.12)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.11em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:6.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="95.32" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="499.66"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.11em;">
<span id="Thmclaim2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmclaim2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim 2</span></span><span id="Thmclaim2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="Thmclaim2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="Thmclaim2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmclaim2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Weight update in low-precision training is biased by <math id="Thmclaim2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]{\mathbf{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝛅</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝛅</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐑</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]{\mathbf{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which arises from the structurally similar matrices (denoted as <math id="Thmclaim2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐑</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>) across tokens and training steps, and its positively-biased coefficient <math id="Thmclaim2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝛅</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝛅</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]</annotation></semantics></math>. This bias accumulates error, preventing cancellation, increasing weight spectral norm and activation, and leading to loss explosion.</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F5.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.04212v1/cumsum_of_D_diff.svg" id="S3.F5.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:176/140;" width="176" height="140"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Positively-biased <math id="S3.F5.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}\!-\!{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.052em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}\!-\!{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F5.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.04212v1/o_do_visualization.svg" id="S3.F5.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:176/141;" width="176" height="141"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Large values in features 20 &amp; 29</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F5.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.04212v1/o_diff_do_visualization.svg" id="S3.F5.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:176/142;" width="176" height="142"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>Large error in features 20 &amp; 29</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Analysis of <math id="S3.F5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\delta}}=\mathrm{rowsum}(d{\mathbf{O}}\circ{\mathbf{O}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜹</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>rowsum</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐎</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>𝐎</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\delta}}=\mathrm{rowsum}(d{\mathbf{O}}\circ{\mathbf{O}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.3.2 </span>Cause 2. Biased Rounding Error Leads to Positive <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section investigates the origin of the positive bias in <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]</annotation></semantics></math>. We trace this error to the interaction between <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d{\mathbf{O}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐎</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d{\mathbf{O}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the numerical discrepancy in <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{O}}_{lp}-{\mathbf{O}}_{hp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{O}}_{lp}-{\mathbf{O}}_{hp}</annotation></semantics></math>, which itself arises from biased rounding errors in BF16 addition during the <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}{\mathbf{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}{\mathbf{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> computation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S3.F6.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.04212v1/P_V_visualization.svg" id="S3.F6.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:176/141;" width="176" height="141"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Most <math id="S3.F6.sf1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{V}}[:,i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{V}}[:,i]</annotation></semantics></math> are negative</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S3.F6.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.04212v1/o_error_visualization.svg" id="S3.F6.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:176/141;" width="176" height="141"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Large error when <math id="S3.F6.sf2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}[T,i]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}[T,i]=1</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S3.F6.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.04212v1/detail_view_standalone.svg" id="S3.F6.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:176/141;" width="176" height="141"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>Detailed view of (b)</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Analysis of <math id="S3.F6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}{\mathbf{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}{\mathbf{V}}</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Locate the Large Error in <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]</annotation></semantics></math></h5>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first investigate the source of the positive bias in <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{T=1}^{N}({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{T=1}^{N}({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]</annotation></semantics></math>. As analyzed in <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Isolating the Source of Failure within Flash Attention ‣ 3 Root Causes of Instability in Flash Attention ‣ Why Low-Precision Transformer Training Fails: An Analysis on Flash Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, the error in <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\delta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜹</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\delta}}</annotation></semantics></math> stems from the product of the upstream gradient <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d{\mathbf{O}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐎</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d{\mathbf{O}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the numerical error in the low-precision output, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{O}}_{lp}-{\mathbf{O}}_{hp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{O}}_{lp}-{\mathbf{O}}_{hp}</annotation></semantics></math>. To dissect this, we focus on a token position <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=718" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>718</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=718</annotation></semantics></math> where the error component <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{\delta}}_{lp}-{\bm{\delta}}_{hp})[T]</annotation></semantics></math> is positive.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#S3.F5" title="In Similar Low-rank Updates of Weight Cause Training Failure ‣ 3.3.1 Cause 1. Similar Low-Rank Matrices Bias Weight Updates ‣ 3.3 The Root Causes of Training Failure ‣ 3 Root Causes of Instability in Flash Attention ‣ Why Low-Precision Transformer Training Fails: An Analysis on Flash Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>(b) and (c), we observe a strong sign correlation between the gradient <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d{\mathbf{O}}[T,:]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d{\mathbf{O}}[T,:]</annotation></semantics></math> and the output error <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{O}}_{lp}[T,:]-{\mathbf{O}}_{hp}[T,:]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{O}}_{lp}[T,:]-{\mathbf{O}}_{hp}[T,:]</annotation></semantics></math> for specific feature dimensions such as 20 and 29 (also observed across other tokens). In these dimensions, both <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d{\mathbf{O}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐎</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d{\mathbf{O}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the output error <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{O}}_{lp}-{\mathbf{O}}_{hp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{O}}_{lp}-{\mathbf{O}}_{hp}</annotation></semantics></math> are consistently negative. This alignment ensures their product, which contributes to the error in <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\delta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜹</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\delta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, is positive. The fact that the output error tends to be negative (<math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{O}}_{lp}[T,i]&lt;{\mathbf{O}}_{hp}[T,i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{O}}_{lp}[T,i]&lt;{\mathbf{O}}_{hp}[T,i]</annotation></semantics></math>) indicates that the low-precision computation of <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{O}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{O}}</annotation></semantics></math> is systematically biased towards more negative values. Our subsequent analysis, therefore, focuses on identifying the origin of this computational bias.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The output <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{O}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{O}}</annotation></semantics></math> is computed from an intermediate unnormalized output, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\mathbf{O}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\mathbf{O}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The computation involves a safe softmax followed by a matrix multiplication and normalization:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\exp({\mathbf{S}}-\mathrm{rowmax}({\mathbf{S}}))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>rowmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\exp({\mathbf{S}}-\mathrm{rowmax}({\mathbf{S}})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{{\mathbf{O}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{{\mathbf{O}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}{\mathbf{V}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}{\mathbf{V}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbf{O}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbf{O}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bar{{\mathbf{O}}}/\mathrm{rowsum}(\bar{{\mathbf{P}}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>rowsum</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bar{{\mathbf{O}}}/\mathrm{rowsum}(\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Further experiments pinpoint the source of failure to the computation of the unnormalized output, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\mathbf{O}}}=\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}{\mathbf{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\mathbf{O}}}=\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}{\mathbf{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We find that computing only this product in FP32 is sufficient to stabilize training. To understand the origin of this bias, we examine the difference between the low-precision and high-precision computation of a single element, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\mathbf{O}}}[T,i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\mathbf{O}}}[T,i]</annotation></semantics></math> (for feature index <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=20</annotation></semantics></math> in our analysis):</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bar{{\mathbf{O}}}_{lp}[T,i]-\bar{{\mathbf{O}}}_{hp}[T,i]=(\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}_{lp}[T,:]{\mathbf{V}}[:,i])_{lp}-(\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}_{hp}[T,:]{\mathbf{V}}[:,i])_{hp}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\mathbf{O}}}_{lp}[T,i]-\bar{{\mathbf{O}}}_{hp}[T,i]=(\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}_{lp}[T,:]{\mathbf{V}}[:,i])_{lp}-(\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}_{hp}[T,:]{\mathbf{V}}[:,i])_{hp}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where the inputs <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐕</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> are themselves the results of prior BF16 operations. Specifically, the subscript <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\cdot)_{lp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\cdot)_{lp}</annotation></semantics></math> here computes dot product in FP32 with the final result rounded to BF16, while <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\cdot)_{hp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\cdot)_{hp}</annotation></semantics></math> computes entirely in FP32.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To understand how the error <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\mathbf{O}}}_{lp}[T,i]-\bar{{\mathbf{O}}}_{hp}[T,i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\mathbf{O}}}_{lp}[T,i]-\bar{{\mathbf{O}}}_{hp}[T,i]</annotation></semantics></math> becomes systematically negative, we plot the cumulative error as the sum over token positions progresses in <a href="#S3.F6" title="In 3.3.2 Cause 2. Biased Rounding Error Leads to Positive (𝜹_{𝑙⁢𝑝}-𝜹_{ℎ⁢𝑝})⁢[𝑇] ‣ 3.3 The Root Causes of Training Failure ‣ 3 Root Causes of Instability in Flash Attention ‣ Why Low-Precision Transformer Training Fails: An Analysis on Flash Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>(b) and (c):</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\mathbf{O}}}_{\text{error}}(t)=\left(\sum\nolimits_{t^{\prime}=1}^{t}\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}[T,t^{\prime}]{\mathbf{V}}[t^{\prime},i]\right)_{lp}-\left(\sum\nolimits_{t^{\prime}=1}^{t}\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}[T,t^{\prime}]{\mathbf{V}}[t^{\prime},i]\right)_{hp}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>error</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\mathbf{O}}}_{\text{error}}(t)=\left(\sum\nolimits_{t^{\prime}=1}^{t}\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}[T,t^{\prime}]{\mathbf{V}}[t^{\prime},i]\right)_{lp}-\left(\sum\nolimits_{t^{\prime}=1}^{t}\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}[T,t^{\prime}]{\mathbf{V}}[t^{\prime},i]\right)_{hp}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">The figure shows that the error accumulates in significant negative steps. These steps occur at token positions <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> where the corresponding attention probability <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}[T,t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}[T,t]</annotation></semantics></math> is exactly 1 (also observed in other token positions). This happens when the pre-softmax score <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{S}}[T,t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{S}}[T,t]</annotation></semantics></math> is the maximum value in its row, causing <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\exp({\mathbf{S}}[T,t]-\max({\mathbf{S}}[T,:]))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp({\mathbf{S}}[T,t]-\max({\mathbf{S}}[T,:]))</annotation></semantics></math> to evaluate to <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(0)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(0)=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Analysis of Biased Rounding Error</h5>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, the bias arises from the interaction of these unit values with the distribution of the value matrix <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐕</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>. As observed in <a href="#S3.F6" title="In 3.3.2 Cause 2. Biased Rounding Error Leads to Positive (𝜹_{𝑙⁢𝑝}-𝜹_{ℎ⁢𝑝})⁢[𝑇] ‣ 3.3 The Root Causes of Training Failure ‣ 3 Root Causes of Instability in Flash Attention ‣ Why Low-Precision Transformer Training Fails: An Analysis on Flash Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>(a), for the problematic feature dimension <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=20</annotation></semantics></math>, the values of <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{V}}[:,i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{V}}[:,i]</annotation></semantics></math> are predominantly negative. When <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}[T,t]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}[T,t]=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the product <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}[T,t]{\mathbf{V}}[t,i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\mathbf{P}}}[T,t]{\mathbf{V}}[t,i]</annotation></semantics></math> is simply <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{V}}[t,i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{V}}[t,i]</annotation></semantics></math>, a negative BF16 number.
<em id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">A systematic error then occurs when two such negative BF16 numbers are added.</em> In floating-point arithmetic, adding two numbers with the same sign can cause the resulting significand to overflow (e.g., <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{-1.xxxx}+\mathtt{-1.yyyy}=\mathtt{-10.zzzz}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>𝟷</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚡𝚡𝚡𝚡</mi><mo rspace="0em">+</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>𝟷</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>𝚢𝚢𝚢𝚢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>𝟷𝟶</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>𝚣𝚣𝚣𝚣</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{-1.xxxx}+\mathtt{-1.yyyy}=\mathtt{-10.zzzz}</annotation></semantics></math>), requiring a right shift and an exponent increment to re-normalize. The bits shifted out of the 7-bit BF16 fraction determine the rounding direction. When adding two negative numbers, the rounding operation (e.g., round-to-nearest) can introduce a consistent bias.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To illustrate how this rounding bias occurs, consider the addition of two significands that cause an overflow, requiring a right shift for normalization. The bit that is shifted out (the rounding bit) determines the rounding direction. We show all possible additions of the last two 2-bit numbers, where the green bit represents the bit that would be shifted out (the rounding bit):</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="17.12" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 17.12" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,17.12) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(13.75,0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 6.23 L 0 10.89 C 0 14.33 2.79 17.12 6.23 17.12 L 516.27 17.12 C 519.71 17.12 522.5 14.33 522.5 10.89 L 522.5 6.23 C 522.5 2.79 519.71 0 516.27 0 L 6.23 0 C 2.79 0 0 2.79 0 6.23 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 6.23 L 0.69 10.89 C 0.69 13.95 3.17 16.42 6.23 16.42 L 516.27 16.42 C 519.33 16.42 521.81 13.95 521.81 10.89 L 521.81 6.23 C 521.81 3.17 519.33 0.69 516.27 0.69 L 6.23 0.69 C 3.17 0.69 0.69 3.17 0.69 6.23 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 17.82 8.92)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:35.19em;--ltx-fo-height:0.44em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.44em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.27" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.12)" width="486.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S3.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:35.19em;">
<span id="S3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_centering ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<span id="S3.Ex3"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathtt{00}+\mathtt{00}=\mathtt{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝟶𝟶</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝟶𝟶</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝟶</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathtt{00}+\mathtt{00}=\mathtt{0}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{0,1,0}\mathtt{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#00FF00;" mathcolor="#00FF00">𝟶</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{0,1,0}\mathtt{0}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
